## GO-4 — the review diff ratio across all four rounds, recorded including where nothing was cut

Measured per round against `repo.max_diff_bytes` = 200,000, from the branch rather than from a report:

| Round | Diff bytes | Kept | Share seen | Files with NO patch at all |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 187,685 | 187,685 | **100%** | none — no truncation notice fired |
| 2 | 203,923 | 200,000 | 98.1% | none; the tail of `packages/shared/src/wire.ts` cut mid-file |
| 3 | 219,935 | 200,000 | 90.9% | **2** — `packages/shared/src/wire.ts`, `wire.test.ts` |
| 4 | 227,285 | 200,000 | 87.9% | **5** — the two above plus `packages/server/src/read.test.ts`, `packages/server/src/wire.ts`, `packages/shared/src/docs.test.ts` |

**The share seen falls monotonically as the loop converges**, which is Q-0017's finding reproduced: the
longer a revise loop runs the less each successive reviewer sees, and what it loses is the
alphabetical tail — here `packages/shared/src/wire.ts`, which is AC-8's and AC-9's own subject. The
prediction GO-4 required was made before round 2 and was right about the direction and wrong about
round 1, which is why the obligation says to record the ratio **including when nothing was cut**.

**Rounds 3 and 4 both disclosed it through Q-0117's channel and read the omitted files off the
branch**, in an `observation:` entry naming each file. That is Q-0124's warn and Q-0117's observation
composing for the fourth consecutive ticket (Q-0016, Q-0129, Q-0130, this) — the warn changing what
the reviewer did rather than only recording a gap.

**The claim was verified rather than trusted** (Q-0016's precedent). A hand pass over every omitted
file found **one** thing, and it is the only finding of this pass: `wireRunHistorySchema`'s rollup
element declares `cost_usd: z.number().nullable()` with no range constraint while `unpriced_steps`
and `step_count` beside it carry `.int().nonnegative()`. Q-0017's class and Q-0127 AC-14(a)'s
precedent, fixed by hand after the gate.

Checked and explicitly **not** raised: `step_count` is `.nonnegative()` where its own JSDoc says
"never zero", because AC-9's *Test:* clause specifies non-negative and the schema is a deliberately
loose projection of a document `core` writes and may widen.

## GO-5 — discharged by running the product, and this is what it rendered

Performed 2026-09-18 in Chrome against a daemon started by `quorum open` from the merged integration
worktree, on `http://127.0.0.1:7717`. The served bundle was verified to carry this change's own copy
before anything was clicked, because a cache hit can serve a page built from code nobody is looking
at. Transcribed from the page, not from a report.

**The dry walk, started from the ticket page's own checkbox** — §0.2's hazard demonstrated closed
rather than argued. The page offered one flow (`requirements`, the only one consuming `draft`) and
confirmed before acting: *"Walk requirements on Q-0137 as a dry run? Nothing is invoked, nothing is
written and no lock is taken."* Mission control then rendered:

    Mission control   Run 1   requirements · Q-0137 · ended
    This run is a dry walk: it invoked no adapter and wrote no run history, so nothing was
    recorded for this page to measure.
    Elapsed time is unavailable because the run's history, which records when it started, has
    not been read.
    Per-vendor cost and token totals are unavailable because the run's history, which records
    them, has not been read.

**The network is the proof, not the sentence.** With tracking armed, pressing *Check again* — the one
control that re-reads on a normal run — issued exactly **one** request, `GET /runs/run-1`, and **no
`/history` request at all**. The browser held `ticketId: Q-0137` and `runId: 1`, which is everything
needed to compose `Q-0137-1`, and declined because the wire now carries `dry: true`.

**The hazard itself, shown in the product**: the dry walk rendered **Run 1** and wrote no run history;
the real run that followed also rendered **Run 1** and created `.quorum/runs/Q-0137-1`. Without AC-8
the first screen would have read the second run's manifest and shown its figures as the walk's.
Afterwards the ticket still read `stage draft` with *"no run has written one"* for its run log, which
is *"A dry run changes nothing the caller passed it"* (2026-09-11) holding at the same time.

**The real run, while running** — started through the daemon from the same control, because a
`quorum run` is a different process the host can never see (Q-0121):

    Mission control   Run 1   requirements · Q-0137 · running
    Elapsed  00:13   measured by this browser's clock against the start the run recorded
    Cost per vendor
    No vendor has finished a billed step on this run, so its roll-up names none. A vendor that
    has run without finishing one is absent from it rather than free.
    This run is still in flight: these figures are as of the last read and omit whatever the
    step now running has not been billed for.

Elapsed advanced **00:02 → 00:13 → 00:29** with no page action, while *"Loaded from the daemon, as of
2026-09-18T12:43:32.911Z"* stayed put — **elapsed advances and cost does not**, which is §A.2's entire
design visible in one frame. Pressing *Check again* moved that timestamp to `12:44:00.354Z` and only
then did the rows change: one read on mount, one per explicit refresh, and none on a timer.

**Two vendors, one priced and one not**, after the refresh — and the one-row-then-two transition
review round 1's major was about:

    Cost per vendor
    zeta    $0.020
    omega   reported no price: 2286 tokens, which is unpriced rather than free.
    2 of its counted steps reported no price, so this figure is short by whatever they cost.

**No figure is summed across vendors anywhere, and no `$0.00` appears.** The trace columns
corroborate the header arithmetic independently: `zeta` $0.010 × 2 = $0.020, and `omega`'s two
unpriced calls report 1053 + 1233 = 2286 tokens.

**The same screen after the run ended**, the gate answered `abort` through the gate screen:

    Mission control   Run 1   requirements · Q-0137 · ended
    The run has finished.
    Elapsed  00:56   measured by the engine when the run finished

**The attribution changes with the source** — *"by this browser's clock against the start the run
recorded"* while live, *"by the engine when the run finished"* once ended, which is `duration_ms`
rather than a browser subtraction (§0.3). **The figure is frozen**: still `00:56` eight seconds later,
where it had moved every second while running. The in-flight sentence is gone and both vendor rows
remain, which is AC-17's conditional rendering.

**What was real and what was mocked, stated rather than blurred.** Real: the daemon, the served
bundle, the engine, the flow, the backward edge exhausting at limit 1, the gate question and its
`abort`, `GET /runs/:handle`, `GET /history/:id`, the WebSocket, and the browser. Mocked: the
**vendor CLI** only, through the shipped mock adapter, with per-role profiles naming vendors this
product has never seen (`zeta`, `omega`) so that no rendering could pass by branching on `claude` or
`codex` — which is §0.6's corpus trap avoided in the demonstration as well as in the fixtures.

**Cleaned up, and the one part that was not is stated rather than claimed**: the daemon is stopped
and `harness/harness.yaml` is restored to zero diff. The scratch ticket
`backlog/Q-0137-go-5-header-demonstration` and its run directory `.quorum/runs/Q-0137-1`, both inside
the integration worktree, were **not** removed — the deletion was refused by this environment and was
handed to the maintainer rather than worked around. **Neither can reach `main`**: the first is
untracked, so no merge carries it, and the second is under a gitignored path. Both are named here so
the leftover is visible rather than discovered.
